-- Negative test (found with ako/mxcli#1451): a Java action that returns a
-- StringTemplate must be REFUSED (MDL-JA03).
--
-- A text template is a parameter type only: a Java action's return type is a
-- CodeActions$Type, and CodeActions$StringTemplateParameterType is not one.
-- A unit patched to return one does not load in mxbuild 11.13 ("Type
-- Mendix.Modeler.CodeActions.StringTemplateParameterType does not contain a
-- constructor with a parameter of type Mendix.Modeler.JavaActions.JavaAction").
-- main wrote this statement as a Boolean action without a word: the return
-- converter's default turned every type it did not handle into Boolean. That
-- default is now an error; only an omitted `returns` is Boolean.

mdl 1;

create module BugTestJaRet1451;

create java action BugTestJaRet1451.JA_Subject (Code: String) returns StringTemplate(Text)
as $$
return null;
$$;
